iting  when we  found out that ali and joe were doing  that for us after having two kids  naturally tracy tested positive for hd  do you think  about if symptoms did start soon  what that means for your family are you  able to even process that i think about  it and it feels like a little bit of a  cloud  over you all the time because you never  know when something's gonna hit  the average age is 30 to 50 for symptoms  and i'm 33. she knows  what it most likely looked like for her  and it's really really difficult to see  just always in the back of our mind and  then with any future kids it was like a  huge factor for us in having children  too you rather would not have kids than  pass on this gene right  then they discovered help cure hd  in 2020 they were accepted for a grant  to cover the roughly 20 thousand dollar  cost of having a baby and in september  josiah was born hd free he doesn't know  it but he's not going to have that worry  in his life he might have it for his  family but not for himself and not for  his future family  it's those success stories that fuel  ally and joe  with all these families that you talked  about that you've helped are these now  friendships  and bonds in a way with some of them at  least close with yeah you're getting  closer with some of them bonds which  they say help them stay motivated as  they continue their own journey the man  behind the needle one thing i struggle  with is his happiness i want him to be  happy when i know that we'll have kids  without huntington's disease i know that  if he died tomorrow he would die in  peace knowing that  period  on march 9th ally and joe got one step  closer  that's pregnant right  yes ma'am okay  they are pregnant right now they're very  early along now allie's only six weeks  along right now i just was texting with  her yesterday she's feeling good and the  reason she shares so early because  people normally don't is what she said  in the piece you can't just share the  good this is 